-- title:
--   Height- and length-controlled digital carry homotopies
-- statement:
--   For a base $m\in\mathbb N$, the positive word predicate at height bound $K$ and displacement $n$ is generated by the empty word of displacement zero, the letter $a$ of displacement one, concatenation, conjugation $w\mapsto twt^{-1}$ which multiplies displacement by $m$ and raises height by one, and enlargement of the height bound. A safe homotopy between such words uses presentation-cell moves in context, with every intermediate word retaining the same positive shape and length at most $B$. For $m\ge2$ and $n<R$,
--   $$W_m(n)a\simeq_{\rm safe}W_m(n+1),\qquad
--   K=\lfloor\log_mR\rfloor,\quad B=(m+1)(K+1)+m+3,$$
--   where $W_m(n)$ is the compressed base-$m$ word. This keeps the carry deformation within one finite carrier and one logarithmic length bound.
-- source:
--   Ruijun Wang, Continuous graph homomorphisms of higher dimensional abelian group actions, arXiv:2609.39824v1 (30 September 2026), Sections 2–7, supporting construction for Theorem 1.4 and Proposition 7.1; https://arxiv.org/html/2609.39824v1. Formalization-specific infrastructure in the import closure; individual helper assertions are not represented as separately numbered paper theorems. Original Lean module AbelianTargets/SafeDigitalCarries.lean, selected declaration lines 14-21, 23-26, 28-45, 47-57, 67-74, 76-84, 86-90, 92-111, 113-234, 236-244; SHA-256 3b342b8b5d15f028060791d6ae3c370ef0c67710ca4bf6725b2b40f4328e79a2. Selected spans are from the final generated manifest. The original source snapshot is local; no public repository URL or commit was available.

